# Never hardwire the three games

Words: [README.md — Words used](../../README.md#words-used-in-this-project).
This is **copy 1** of “acceptance titles are tests, not the ISA”
(copy 2: [docs/GAME_DESIGN.md](../../docs/GAME_DESIGN.md)).

The machine **RUNS any compiled HTML**. `INVADERS.HTML` / `PACMAN.HTML` /
`DONKEY.HTML` are acceptance tests, not the instruction set.

**Forbidden:** title names/stems as gates; hardcoded key maps; maze/alien/DK
constants; buffers sized to one title; “for PACMAN” comments to skip JS
semantics (heap/generation cheats: `one-heap-keep-gen`).

**Required:** grow language + VM (closures, timers, `String.replace` + RegExp,
`JSON.stringify`/`parse`, heap lifetimes). Caps are VM-wide with loud overflow.
FAT/load wait scales with ProgramImage bytes, not a title name.
**Version 2.0** for `MK.HTML` is measured numbers, not a title gate —
[html-game-v1.mdc](html-game-v1.mdc) and
[docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md](../../docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md) § Version 1.0 vs 2.0.

